# Phase 7 — Frontend ↔ Flask integration

Do this work when wiring the React app off `frontend/src/data/api.ts` onto Flask `/api/v1`.
Backend contract gaps from `backendaudit.md` that are **frontend-only** live here — do not invent parallel mock behaviour.

## Env / HTTP client

- Add `VITE_API_BASE` (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:5000`) and `VITE_USE_MOCK_API` (default true until cutover).
- All non-public calls: `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`.
- Never send `actor` in bodies/query — JWT supplies actor for audits/lifecycle.

## Auth / session

- Persist **`accessToken` + `AuthUser`** (not AuthUser alone). Clear both on logout.
- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` → `{ accessToken, user }`. Map into Redux/session.
- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` **must send `password`** (UI already collects it; `registerUser` currently drops it).
- Profile: `GET/PATCH /api/v1/auth/me` (AccountPage). Do not call a missing `/users/:id` for self.
- Magic-link / passwordless confirm flow: bridge to password login or disable until Phase 8 — Flask requires password.
- Register password min length is **6** on the API (matches SignUp UI).

## List pagination (breaking vs mock arrays)

These endpoints return a **page envelope**, not a bare array:

```json
{ "items": [...], "total": 0, "limit": 50, "offset": 0, "hasMore": false }
```

- `GET /api/v1/incidents` → use `.items` in `incidentApi.getAll` (or unwrap in HTTP layer).
- `GET /api/v1/admin/audit-logs` → same for `adminApi.getAuditLogs`.
- `GET /api/v1/notifications` → same for `notificationApi.getAll`.
- `GET /api/v1/admin/users` → `adminApi.getUsers` (was a GAP; now exists).

Pass `limit` / `offset` from inbox/tables; default page size 50 (max 200).

## Path / shape adapters

| Frontend | Flask | Adapter |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `handoffApi.getAll` | `GET /api/v1/admin/handoffs` | Map URL under **admin**, not `/handoffs` |
| `removeMedia` boolean | `DELETE …/media/:id` → **204** | Map 204 → `true`; 404 → `false` |
| `markAllAsRead` number | `{ count }` | Return `body.count` |
| Toast errors | Smorest `{ message }` / validation | Normalize to string for toasts |
| Review/detail N+1 GETs | Prefer `GET /api/v1/incidents/:id/detail` | One round-trip: incident + history + notes + media + verification(s) + handoffs |

## Public map privacy

`GET /incidents/active` and `/community` strip reporter contact PII (`reporterEmail`, `reporterPhone`, etc. are null). Map popups must not expect contact fields.

## Notifications create

`POST /api/v1/notifications` (ADMIN) exists for ops enqueue. Lifecycle already creates IN_APP rows server-side — do not double-create from the UI after moderation actions.

## Realtime / Phase 8 (do not block Phase 7)

- No WebSocket/SSE/Realtime yet. Ship refetch-on-mutation + optional short polling for the notification badge.
- Geocode / weather stay browser → Open-Meteo until Flask proxies exist.
- Media: stop uploading huge data URLs once Supabase Storage is wired; API currently accepts URL strings only.

